# Core Security & Secrets

- **Secrets:** No API keys/tokens/passwords in source or git. Gemini only via `apiKeyService` / Settings; AES-GCM as implemented. Local helper variables only via the `.env`/`.env.example` pattern — never commit keys.
- **Frontend env:** In Vite/SPA, `VITE_*` values are client-visible; never put real secrets there.
- **IndexedDB/Dexie:** User data client-side only; never persist secrets outside the dedicated key management.
- **External calls:** Route through existing services (`geminiService`, `pubmedUtils`, `arxivUtils`, RTK slices); no fetch URLs with embedded credentials.
- **Errors:** User-facing messages via i18n; never leak stack traces/IDs in the UI; no sensitive logging in production.
- **HTML/Markdown:** Sanitize as already established in the project (DOMPurify); no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` outside the existing reviewed pattern.

See `@src/services/apiKeyService.ts`, `@AGENTS.md`, `@.env.example`.
